From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:08:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dhtmled.ocx: control properties, document load/save, events,
 OLE object and persistence

The DHTMLEdit control keeps its documented properties (flags, appearance, snap grid, base URL)
with their defaults and holds the document source: NewDocument, DocumentHTML, DocumentTitle,
LoadDocument/LoadURL (files, UTF-8/UTF-16/ANSI), SaveDocument, IsDirty, CurrentDocumentPath,
FilterSourceCode (pass-through), DOM (a separate HTML document with the source). DocumentComplete
is sent to the connected event sinks (connection point Advise/Unadvise/GetConnectionInterface).
IOleObject (class id, user type, verbs, advise holder, moniker from the client site),
IPersistStreamInit (HTML source stream), IPersistStorage class id/dirty, IOleControl and
IViewObject advise no longer fail.

